      "content": "When everything feels like too much effort, the desire to simply quit is completely understandable. If the idea of appointments feels like another overwhelming obligation, perhaps you could start with very small, low-effort acts of self-care today. Even a five-minute walk without a specific goal, or listening to a piece of music that requires no active engagement, can sometimes create a tiny pocket of quiet. Be gentle with yourself; right now, stopping the fight doesn't mean stopping all life, but easing the pressure.",
